            <ArticleTitle>Managing uterine artery pseudoaneurysm after myomectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/uog.18963</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A pseudoaneurysm is a blood-filled cavity communicating with the lumen of the artery and surrounding perivascular tissue creates a wall of pseudoaneurysm. Uterine artery pseudoaneurysm (UAP) after myomectomy is considered a rare and potentially life-threatening event1 .</AbstractText>
